## Overview

Ark is a new nearline storage service provided by YCRC.  It is intended for safe storage of research data on the scale of multiple Terabytes.  Faculty can request an allocation for their group at a cost.  It is NOT designed for direct computation by YCRC’s clusters.  Instead, data must be staged from Ark, to a YCRC cluster, using globus.  Ark is also accessible on your own computers via a network mount.  Controlled access data (HIPAA, NIST 800-171) may not be stored on Ark.

## FAQ

**How much does Ark cost?**

Ark costs $2/TiB/month for allocated quota.  You are charged for that quota whether or not you are using it.  This charge covers two copies of your data.

**How will I be charged for Ark storage?**

You will receive a monthly statement that details your allocated quota and the associated charge.  

**How do I request Ark space?**  
Only PI’s (faculty) can request space on Ark.  Other members of the group can be given access to the space on request.

Please fill out \<website link\>.  You will be asked for the following information:

- Valid COA for charging  
- NetIDs of all group members who should have access  
- The requested quota.  We are currently limiting quotas to 10-100 TiBs until we have more capacity.  

**How safe are my data on Ark?**

Your data are very safe.  We maintain two copies; one in MGHPCC, and one in West Campus.  This protects against major system failure.  In addition, Ark maintains a week of snapshots, which protects against inadvertent deletion.

**How do I access data on Ark?**

Ark is available in three ways:

* Globus:    
  * Use the Ark Globus Endpoint, and navigate to /\<sharename\>.  We will confirm with you your \<sharename\> after approval of your Ark storage request.   
  * From there you can stage data to Bouchet cluster storage (e.g. scratch) or transfer to other endpoints.  
* Mount your Ark storage on your own computer.    
  * Windows: Mount \\\\ark.ycrc.yale.edu\\\<sharename\> using yale\\netid as username and your netid password.  
  * Mac: In Finder, Use the “Go \-\> Connect to server” and enter \`smb://ark.ycrc.yale.edu/\<sharename\>\` as a “registered user” and use your netid/password to authenticate  
* Command-line via smbclient  
  * smbclient //ark.ycrc.yale.edu/sharename \-U netID \-W Yale 

**What can I store on Ark?**

Ark is for low and moderate risk data only, as defined by [Yale’s MSS](https://cybersecurity.yale.edu/data-classification).  No high risk data may be stored on Ark. →.no hippa or nist

HIPPA and NIST 800-171 data is prohibited on Ark. All other data can be stored on Ark. For more details, please refer to [Yale’s MSS](https://cybersecurity.yale.edu/data-classification).

**What is Ark’s Service Level Agreement (SLA)?**

While we will make an effort to minimize downtimes, we cannot guarantee 100% availability.  In particular, MGHPCC has a yearly full outage that typically lasts at least one day, during which Ark will not be available. In addition, YCRC may perform routine maintenance that could disrupt access. YCRC provides ample communication in advance of planned downtimes to our users so that you can plan accordingly.

